  <body>
    <main>
      <article aria-labelledby="title">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">A short note about long text</p>
          <h1 id="title"><span>AI</span><b>;</b>DR</h1>
          <p class="expansion">AI; Don't Read</p>
        </header>

        <p class="principle">
          AI-generated text should not be longer than what you would have written yourself <em>pre-AI</em>.
        </p>

        <div class="argument">
          <p>AI made writing cheap.</p>
          <p>It did not make reading free.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="consequence">
          Otherwise, we will ask AI to shorten AI-generated long texts.
          Something will get lost in translation.
          Whose fault will that be—and what was the point of the long text?
        </p>

        <section aria-labelledby="before-sending">
          <h2 id="before-sending">Before sending</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Cut the warm-up.</li>
            <li>Keep the point.</li>
            <li>Make the decision clear.</li>
            <li>Respect the reader's time.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <footer>
